00:29:08.090 --> 00:29:10.465
So for those people who aren't
familiar with Google Cloud

00:29:10.465 --> 00:29:12.290
Shell, this is a really
cool little thing

00:29:12.290 --> 00:29:14.238
that if you go into the
Google Cloud console,

00:29:14.238 --> 00:29:16.280
there's a little icon that
looks like a terminal.

00:29:16.280 --> 00:29:18.300
Click that, and
inside your browser,

00:29:18.300 --> 00:29:20.840
it will pop up a terminal
that has basically all

00:29:20.840 --> 00:29:22.970
the standard tooling that
you need for doing just

00:29:22.970 --> 00:29:26.450
about anything, so G
Cloud, Git, Go, Python, et

00:29:26.450 --> 00:29:27.710
cetera, et cetera.

00:29:27.710 --> 00:29:28.600
It's super handy.

00:29:28.600 --> 00:29:29.630
It persists.

00:29:29.630 --> 00:29:31.462
If your home
directory ever resets

00:29:31.462 --> 00:29:33.170
and if you come back
to it after a while,

00:29:33.170 --> 00:29:35.810
it will bring all the stuff
back again for a period of time.

00:29:35.810 --> 00:29:36.770
Really, really handy stuff.

00:29:36.770 --> 00:29:38.270
But you might find
there are scenarios

00:29:38.270 --> 00:29:39.812
where you're like,
wow, I really wish

00:29:39.812 --> 00:29:42.110
I could access my Cloud
Shell from the terminal just

00:29:42.110 --> 00:29:43.340
on my local machine.

00:29:43.340 --> 00:29:45.240
There's a bunch of different
tools that are available now.

00:29:45.240 --> 00:29:47.282
They're in alpha, but you
will have links to them

00:29:47.282 --> 00:29:48.050
in the show notes.

00:29:48.050 --> 00:29:50.390
If you run G Cloud
alpha Cloud Shell SSH,

00:29:50.390 --> 00:29:52.850
it will SSH into your
Cloud Shell terminal

00:29:52.850 --> 00:29:55.400
and make it available locally,
basically through SSH,

00:29:55.400 --> 00:29:56.720
which is super, super nice.

00:29:56.720 --> 00:29:59.450
You can also use the G Cloud
alpha Cloud Shell commands

00:29:59.450 --> 00:30:01.250
to SSP files up
and down, so if you

00:30:01.250 --> 00:30:02.945
want to bring local
files to the machine

00:30:02.945 --> 00:30:04.070
or bring them down as well.

00:30:04.070 --> 00:30:06.200
But the thing that gets
me actually really excited

00:30:06.200 --> 00:30:09.860
is that the G Cloud alpha Cloud
Shell command has a Get Mount

00:30:09.860 --> 00:30:10.410
