00:30:10.410 --> 00:30:13.010
So if you're running
Linux or Mac OS, basically

00:30:13.010 --> 00:30:15.530
anything that can
support SSHFS, it'll

00:30:15.530 --> 00:30:18.410
give you the command to mount
your Cloud Shell locally,

00:30:18.410 --> 00:30:19.745
using SSHFS.

00:30:19.745 --> 00:30:20.870
I think this is super cool.

00:30:20.870 --> 00:30:22.160
Because maybe if you're
running on a machine--

00:30:22.160 --> 00:30:23.618
